{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and It's Entertainment appeal to me because polished, expressive vocal performances feel like a natural continuation of A Musical Affair, Stages, and Lead With Your Heart.",
    "Cinema and Wicked connect with my interest in music that tells a story through film or theatre; Cinema feels especially promising given my soundtrack listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect to something I have listened to before, but I want everyday listening now, so that connection does not make them immediate choices.",
    "The Very Best Of, Born Again: Miracles Edition, and The World in My Mind give me too little evidence of the vocal or soundtrack qualities I want to choose them over clearer matches."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for more holiday music, although that interest depends on my listening mood.",
    "A broad connection to my past albums is not enough by itself; I need a recognizable connection to the singing or musical storytelling I enjoy."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The recurring appeal of expressive vocals and theatrical performances across several of my past choices matters more to me now than the holiday theme of a few recordings.",
    "My soundtrack listening and interest in Stages make film-themed music and full cast recordings appealing next steps, beyond simply finding another similar album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in expressive vocals and musical storytelling, but gave too much weight to past holiday listening and some uncertain connections."
}"}
